{
  "abstract": "Unconditional Lean 4 + Mathlib formalization (zero sorry, zero native_decide, standard axioms only) settling Conjecture 5.1 of Bevan, Homberger, and Tenner (JCTA 153, 2018) for every odd k = 2m - 1 >= 1 in its taxicab-breadth formulation: at minimal size n = 2m^2 + 2m and modulus N = 2m^2 + 2m + 1, a permutation w of Fin n has taxicab breadth at least d = 2m + 1 iff w(i) + 1 = +(2m + 1)(i + 1) (mod N) or w(i) + 1 = -(2m + 1)(i + 1) (mod N) for all i, giving exactly 2 valid permutations forming a single D_4 symmetry orbit. Also formalizes the 2D radius-m Lee-sphere tiling classification (every tiling of Z^2 containing (0, 0) equals LambdaPlus m or LambdaMinus m) and the even-k factorial lower bound 2 * (r - 1)! = 2 * (k/2)! at n = 2r^2 - 1, d = 2r for every r >= 2. Equivalence between taxicab breadth >= k + 2 and k-prolific permutations (plus minimal size m(k)) is cited from Bevan, Homberger, and Tenner (2018, Theorem 2.25 and Corollary 4.3). Companion page, dated preprint (2026-11-23-v1), verification archive, and prior-work search logs are published at https://mathdiscoveries.org/results/minimal-prolific-permutations. Generated and checked by AI research agents built and directed by Tyler B. Hughes. No human mathematician has yet refereed the proof.",
